			<div class="content" id="post-content-4826489">
									

<p><strong>Seeking Greenlights:</strong> Yes</p>
<p><strong>Page Type:</strong> SCP Article</p>
<p><strong>Genre (Optional):</strong> Horror<br />
<strong>Page Layout (Optional):</strong> Description, then going into the bread crumb trail that leads up to finding it and piecing together what lead up to it. Mysterious depths all connecting to one club, getting to the club they use emails and notes and security footage to piece together what initially happened.</p>
<p><strong>Elevator Pitch:</strong> A Djinn like creature that eats the consciousness of people lures its victims in with music and pacify them with hallucinogens. As it consumes it becomes stronger and more physical.</p>
<p><strong>Central Narrative:</strong> The central narrative I'm going to follow is a survivor of the stereo's effects, a young man who he and his young adult friends are trying to convert this run down warehouse into some kind of club. Initially, it goes well until his buddy brings in a new blue tooth stereo they found in his attic they found locked in a strongbox. It has a surprising range of sound and usually plays very good music, however they can't seem to get it to play what they want. But the cool steam it releases is a great aesthetic for the club. A few things happen that are weird one of their friends almost ODs, the stereo turns on at random times while he's sleeping there, weird dreams and it moves about but nothing extreme. Night of their grand opening they get a respectable crowd showing up. As the party starts the thing begins producing more steam than ever, and people begin dropping like flies but none of them seem to notice things are going wrong. The whole time he knows somethings wrong he can feel it but even as he collapses and as a shadowy cloud descends over him he can't bring himself to leave. Because it feels so good. And this goes on for a while, and since there are so many people it can just feed of their surface consciousness not killing anyone right away. It becomes more and more physical even becoming an ambiguous member of their crew but no one seems to notice. It's on the last night with their biggest crowd yet that things get bad and it begins gorging itself, and people start dying. Luckily the foundation catches wind and swoops in saving him and four other people out of almost sixty.</p>
<p><strong>Hook/Attention-Grabber:</strong> I want to convey this feeling of the thrill of a party basically, but alongside the feeling that something is not right, and suddenly it's too late you realize that your helpless and that there is no escape from a now looming predator. I think lots of us will understand the hypnotic power of music, I want to give it a literal twist I think.</p>
<p><strong>Additional Notes:</strong> I fear I cannot convey what I'm trying to do with this article properly, but I hope you enjoy what I'm laying now.</p>

							</div>

										<div class="signature">
					<hr class="signature-separator"/>
					

<p>So I didn't know what else to put here so I put a favorite quote, &quot;Who wants to become a writer? And why? Because it’s the answer to everything. … It’s the streaming reason for living. To note, to pin down, to build up, to create, to be astonished at nothing, to cherish the oddities, to let nothing go down the drain, to make something, to make a great flower out of life, even if it’s a cactus.&quot;</p>

				</div>
					
